inner("/privacy/","Privacy Policy | Jarwis","How Jarwis handles your data: no accounts, no ad tracking, and AI messages sent to providers only to answer you.","Privacy policy",f'<section><p>Last updated {TODAY}.</p><h2>What Jarwis collects</h2><p>Jarwis has no accounts and no advertising or analytics trackers. Our hosting provider keeps standard technical logs such as IP address and requested page.</p><h2>AI chats</h2><p>When you chat with Jarwis or an assistant, your message and the last few messages are sent to an AI provider (Groq or Google Gemini) to produce a reply. Jarwis does not save them in a database. Please do not share passwords, ID numbers or other sensitive information. Each provider handles data under its own policy.</p><h2>Resume Builder, cover letters and interview practice</h2><p>The education, skills, projects, experience and job details you enter are sent to the AI provider to write your resume. For the resume, your name, email and phone number are not sent; they are added in your browser. A cover letter request includes your name so the letter can be signed. Interview Practice sends the job title, level, job description and your typed answers. Mission Control sends your goal and the specialist notes.</p><h2>Live data tools</h2><p>When you tap Fetch live data, your browser contacts a public service directly (GitHub, Open-Meteo, Frankfurter, Hacker News, Crossref or Wikipedia). That service can see your IP address and what you searched for. The result is then sent to the AI provider so the assistant can analyse it. Three optional tools (job search, US stock quotes and nutrition) run on the server with the site keys, so your search text goes to that service through Jarwis.</p><h2>On your device</h2><p>Your recent Jarwis chat, saved mission plans, your resume form draft, assistants you create, your theme choice and cached pages are stored in your browser. Clear your site data to remove them.</p><h2>Questions</h2><p>Use the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a>.</p></section>',"Privacy")
inner("/terms/","Terms of Use | Jarwis","The terms for using Jarwis: AI answers can be wrong, are not professional advice, and are provided without warranty.","Terms of use",f'<section><p>Last updated {TODAY}.</p><h2>Using Jarwis</h2><p>Jarwis is provided as is, without warranty, and may change or be unavailable at times. Use it lawfully and do not try to abuse or overload it.</p><h2>AI can be wrong</h2><p>Answers come from AI models and may be inaccurate or out of date. Check important facts yourself. Nothing here is legal, medical, financial or other professional advice.</p><h2>Your content</h2><p>You are responsible for what you type. Do not enter confidential or sensitive information.</p><h2>Contact</h2><p>See the <a href="/contact/">contact page</a> or the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p></section>',"Terms")
