inner("/tools/","Live Data Tools | Jarwis","Free public APIs that give Jarwis assistants real data: GitHub, weather, currency rates, tech news, research papers and Wikipedia. No keys needed.","Live data tools",f'<section><p style="max-width:62ch">34 of the 99 assistants can fetch real data before they answer (42 with the optional keyed sources). Open an assistant on the <a href="/assistants/">assistants page</a>, tap Fetch live data, and it analyses what comes back. All sources are free and need no API key. They were chosen from the community list <a href="https://github.com/public-apis/public-apis" rel="noopener">public-apis</a>, and APIs that now need a key (for example OpenAlex) were left out.</p></section><section><div class="grid">{tt}</div></section><section><h2>Extra sources that need a free key</h2><p>Three more sources switch on when the site owner adds a free key: <strong>Adzuna</strong> job search (for Job & Internship Scout, Resume & Career Coach, LinkedIn Profile Optimizer and Interview Prep Coach), <strong>Finnhub</strong> US stock quotes (for Decision Analyst, Risk Assessor, Scenario Modeler and Cashflow Modeler) and <strong>CalorieNinjas</strong> nutrition (for Wellness Advisor, Fitness &amp; Habit Coach and Shopping Coordinator). Keys stay on the server and are never sent to your browser. The Status page shows which ones are on.</p></section><section><h2>Good to know</h2><p>The calls go straight from your browser to each service, so that service can see your IP address. Live data is only as fresh and complete as the source. Weather data by <a href="https://open-meteo.com/" rel="noopener">Open-Meteo.com</a>.</p></section>',"Live data")
